@startuml senku-sorted-streaming
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
top to bottom direction

title Senku READY Globally Sorted Streaming

frame "Only terminal runs remain when ready.properties is published" {
  folder "Shard S000\none final sorted run" as Source0
  folder "Shard S001\none final sorted run" as Source1
  artifact "..." as SourceMore
  folder "Shard S(m-1)\none final sorted run" as SourceM
}

frame "One sequential cursor per shard containing data" {
  component "Cursor S000" as Cursor0
  component "Cursor S001" as Cursor1
  component "..." as CursorMore
  component "Cursor S(m-1)" as CursorM
}

component "Global merge of at most m inputs\nCompare the head of every\nshard cursor" as GlobalMerge
component "Stream<Entry<K,V>>\nGlobal comparator order\nclose owns all cursors" as Stream
component "SenkuReady.close()\nforcibly closes active stream" as ReadyClose

Source0 --> Cursor0
Source1 --> Cursor1
SourceMore --> CursorMore
SourceM --> CursorM

Cursor0 --> GlobalMerge
Cursor1 --> GlobalMerge
CursorMore --> GlobalMerge
CursorM --> GlobalMerge
GlobalMerge --> Stream
ReadyClose --> Stream : close

note right of GlobalMerge
One stream needs at most m source cursors
and current-part readers. Duplicate keys
were folded during terminal consolidation.
Manifest-only empty runs contribute no cursor.
The directory lock permits only one SenkuReady handle.
That handle permits only one active stream.
Exhaustion, stream close, or ready close releases every cursor.
An internal cursor, storage, or cleanup failure
moves SenkuReady to ERROR.
end note
@enduml
